Go standard-library algorithm references

The new Base32, varint, checksum, slash-path and bit-arithmetic implementations follow
Go 1.26 standard-library conventions and algorithm references, adapted to
GoML's checked results, explicit state and buffer APIs. Relevant source paths
are src/encoding/base32, src/encoding/binary/varint.go, src/hash, and
src/math/bits and src/path in https://github.com/golang/go/tree/go1.26.0.
The upstream copyright and license notice is retained below.

Unicode classification, range, simple case and simple-fold tables are generated
from Go 1.26 src/unicode, pinned to Unicode 15.0.0. The packed representation and
lookup implementation are adapted for GoML; see unicode/DATA.md for regeneration.

Byte split/count/replacement boundary conventions follow src/bytes/bytes.go in
Go 1.26, with GoML Result errors, shared slice views and explicit output limits.

IP value classification, ordering, prefix and byte-conversion contracts follow
Go 1.26 src/net/netip, adapted to existing GoML address families, checked results,
optional neighboring addresses and a separate scoped-address composition.

Portable filesystem traversal follows src/io/fs/walk.go's callback and skip
conventions, adapted to an explicit stack, typed controls, cached names and
bounded work rather than recursive traversal.
Portable glob and link-capability conventions also reference src/io/fs/glob.go
and src/io/fs/readlink.go, with explicit errors, static capabilities and budgets.
The in-memory test filesystem references src/testing/fstest/mapfs.go conventions,
adapted to checked immutable snapshots, pre-indexed directories and bounded
iterative link resolution instead of a caller-mutable map.

